# Upgrade existing rooms where the topic already has a door.
append('twinkle-family-violence',panel('Violence against women: safety and a future',p('Safety, housing, legal help and recovery need to connect. AIHW’s family, domestic and sexual violence evidence separates different forms of harm and reporting sources; a dated survey measure is not an annual 2026 rate. No one needs to disclose their experience to participate in public debate.')+links([('https://www.aihw.gov.au/family-domestic-and-sexual-violence','AIHW: evidence and measures'),('https://www.1800respect.org.au/','1800RESPECT: support')])+opts([('Safe housing and funded support','Emergency shelter and longer-term security make leaving safer. Capacity, accessibility and continuity must extend beyond one night.'),('Accountability and legal assistance','Orders, investigation, legal support and behaviour-change responses need timely enforcement and evaluation. A document alone does not guarantee safety.'),('Prevention and recovery','Schools, workplaces, community leadership and trauma-informed care can address patterns before and after harm. Sustained funding and outcome measures matter more than a one-off campaign.')])+p('housing, care and legal-memory rooms connect these practical layers. Ask representatives about local refuge access, time to legal support and continuity of care. Use private official support routes for personal incidents; this site does not collect identifiable allegations. In immediate danger call 000. The gender pay gap is a distinct topic.')+links([('housing-simulations.html','Housing options'),('aura-clinical-path.html','Recovery and care'),('legal-rag.html','Legal memory'),('gender-pay-gap.html','Separate pay-gap room')])))
f=D/'twinkle-family-violence.html';s=f.read_text(encoding='utf-8').replace('On average a woman a week is killed in this country by a current or former partner, and we still put the person who was hurt on the stand instead of the person who did the hurting.','Violence and coercive control can make home unsafe, and the person who was harmed should not have to carry the burden of fixing the system.');save('twinkle-family-violence',s)
append('tobacco',panel('Tobacco tax: affordability, autonomy and trust',p('People can object to an unaffordable legal habit and distrust government motives while taking health harms seriously. Compare excise objectives with actual affordability, quitting, substitution and distributional effects. Revenue is not the same as health benefit, and enforcement is not the whole conversation.')+opts([('Review the excise path','Compare a pause, redesign or reduction with continued increases. Estimate household costs, consumption, substitution and the public-budget effect, then evaluate rather than assume pass-through.'),('Make support affordable and voluntary','Accessible cessation and health care can expand choice without shaming people. Support should not depend on endorsing a tax policy.'),('Publish the trust ledger','Show revenue, health spending, enforcement costs and measured outcomes on consistent dates. Explain uncertainty in illicit-market estimates rather than dress it up as precision.')])+p('Civic Ledger offers a way to show those tradeoffs. Personal growing and reclassification remain a separate reform debate with their own current-law boundaries.')+links([('price-tax.html','Compare different tax categories'),('restricted-plants.html','Plant prohibition and personal growing reform')])) )
append('restricted-plants',panel('Compare international models without importing their law',p('Oregon’s psilocybin-services model uses licensed service centres and facilitators and sits alongside continuing US federal restrictions. It is a different framework from Australia’s authorised-psychiatrist pathway. Compare access, training, cost, adverse-event reporting and follow-up; a service framework elsewhere does not establish a right to grow or supply in Australia.')+links([('https://www.oregon.gov/oha/ph/preventionwellness/pages/psilocybin-what-are-psilocybin-services.aspx','Oregon Health Authority: how the service model works'),(tga,'Compare Australia’s medical pathway')])))
append('ancient-aliens',panel('Ancient aliens &amp; religion: compare the questions',p('A sacred account, an archaeological object and a modern extraterrestrial hypothesis can ask different things of the same image. Religious traditions also contain internal differences; one translation or television interpretation cannot speak for every believer or custodian. Explore original context, symbolism, transmission and lived meaning alongside material evidence.')+opts([('Historical and archaeological reading','Investigate date, provenance, translation and what the object’s context supports. Missing context should remain visible.'),('Religious and philosophical reading','Ask what the account means within a tradition and how its interpreters understand it. Meaning and spiritual experience are not identical to a testable claim about ancient engineering.'),('Extraordinary physical hypothesis','Identify what specific new evidence would distinguish the hypothesis from cultural symbolism, human achievement or later reinterpretation. An open question is a reason to investigate, not invented confirmation.')])+p('Truth Engine and Sensorium offer a shared evidence room; the Alien Necklace film offers creative exploration. Invite historians, archaeologists, faith communities and cultural custodians into a respectful discussion, with permission for material that is not public.')+links([('truth-engine.html','Claims, interpretations and corrections'),('alien-necklace-film.html','creative doorway')])) )
append('mental-health',panel('A separate doorway for psychedelic care',p('Evidence, supervised access, affordability and clinical safeguards deserve a focused room alongside ordinary care, housing and social support. The authorised pathway is not a guarantee of benefit or a general permission to possess or cultivate controlled substances.')+links([('psychedelic-mental-health.html','Psychedelics for mental health')])))
append('child-safety',panel('Across the wider online world',p('Age-appropriate AI is one part of online safety. Harassment, image-based abuse, privacy, moderation appeals and platform design also affect adults. Those questions have their own room.')+links([('online-safety.html','Online safety for the wider public')])))
append('twinkle-aukus',panel('Three different questions beyond the big receipt',p('International wars asks about force, diplomacy and civilian consequences. Security fallacies tests threat assumptions, dependencies and alternative investments. Migration equations examines population, homes, skills and services. Each has a distinct room.')+links([('international-wars.html','International wars'),('security-fallacies.html','Security fallacies'),('migration-equations.html','Migration equations')])))

